  "worked_solution": "First, we write $8$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n8=\\frac{8}{1}\n$$\n\nTo find the reciprocal of a fraction, we switch the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{8}{1}\\,\\to \\,\\frac{1}{8}\n$$\n\nSo the reciprocal of $8$ is $\\frac{1}{8}.$",
